@packages/core/src/model/source.sigil from SigilSourceModel import { SourceModel }
@packages/core/src/model/diagnostics.sigil from SigilDiagnosticModel import { DiagnosticModel }

component SigilRetrievalModel {
  goal {
    Define immutable purpose-retrieval targets, evidence, graphs, raw results, and
    agent-oriented projections.
  }

  interface {
    RetrievalModel {
      SourceModel and DiagnosticModel provide source and diagnostic data.

      PurposeRetrievalResult and its target, graph, evidence, inclusion, exclusion,
      context, and fingerprint data preserve deterministic retrieval output.
    }

    RetrievalProjection {
      RetrievalProjection is the separately versioned sigil-retrieval-projection/v2
      agent presentation schema derived deterministically from one
      PurposeRetrievalResult.

      RetrievalProjection does not embed or re-export the raw
      sigil-purpose-retrieval/v2 result or its fingerprint. It leaves that result
      unchanged and derives a separate projection fingerprint from its own content.

      RetrievalProjection contains purpose, target, ordered RetrievedComponent
      entries, glossary entries derived from glossary-definition evidence in their
      existing order, diagnostics copied from the raw result in their existing order,
      and a projection fingerprint.

      A projection glossary entry has the canonical term and definition from one
      glossary-definition EvidenceUnit. It does not include occurrence records or
      unused GlossaryFile entries.

      RetrievedComponent has one stable component identity, path, one role,
      component-owned links, and one purpose-appropriate contract projection.
      Multiple relationships use the first role: selected, dependency, importer, then
      cycle-member. Ordinary project summaries follow those same rules when
      explicitly selected or related; directory ancestry introduces no summary role.

      A component-owned link has one relation, an exact target component identity,
      and its available import or annotation location. Links do not require a
      separate presentation-level relationship map.

      A selected component contract groups goal, interface, state, logic,
      constraints, decisions, and cases by their owning component.

      Every RetrievedComponent interface groups SemanticUnits by local grouping Tag
      when a local grouping Tag identity exists and retains ungrouped interface units
      without inventing a Tag.

      A non-selected dependency, importer, or cycle-member contract exposes goal and
      interface in this compact presentation. Complete provider interpretation
      context remains in raw evidence with its original owner and contract roles; a
      budget explicitly discloses withheld context.

      All SemanticUnits remain under their owning component and matching local
      grouping Tag or contract. Repeated grouping occurrences collect additively
      without overriding or duplicating their Facets; no expansion category remains.

      OwnershipLink records an advisory implements, uses, or tests relation, a
      repository-relative one-way implementation location, optional symbol, and
      selected sections. Its owner is the consumer component. Optional annotation Tag
      scope records the exact accessible Tag and its separate originating owner,
      including imported or inline-only Tags. It does not create local grouping or
      prove implementation completeness or alignment.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    RetrievalProjection {
      Projection component identities and links are exact, stable, and resolvable
      within the same projection.

      A raw graph edge whose source or target does not correspond to a projected
      component is omitted from projection links. Every emitted link therefore
      resolves to an entry in the same projection.

      Projection ordering is deterministic. Components sort by selected status, role
      priority, normalized path, declaration start and end location with an absent
      location after a present location, component name, then stable identity; string
      comparisons use Unicode scalar order and numeric locations sort ascending.
      Links sort by relation, target identity, origin path, origin start and end
      location with an absent location after a present location, then stable source
      identity. Section units retain raw evidence order.

      Ordinary project summaries use ordinary component ordering and are never
      duplicated under an additional module-context role.

      Sigil projection locations retain normalized repository-relative paths,
      authoritative half-open UTF-8 byte ranges, and captured source identity.
      Available one-based scalar line/column presentation derives from that snapshot.
      Implementation entrypoint locations keep their separately identified coordinate
      encoding and one-way line/column presentation; neither is mislabeled as a Sigil
      SourceRange.

      A projection fingerprint covers purpose, target, components, glossary entries,
      and diagnostics in their emitted order, excluding the projection fingerprint
      field itself. It does not replace the raw PurposeRetrievalResult fingerprint.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    UnifiedRetrievalModel {
      Decision: Keep evidence-first retrieval and component-first projection in one
      SigilRetrievalModel while versioning their wire contracts separately.

      Scope: Governs semantic model ownership; excludes raw-result and projection
      consumer protocols.

      Rationale: Both contracts share retrieval identities, source locations,
      diagnostics, and deterministic derivation rules.

      Consequences: Consumers can evolve either schema independently while one
      semantic model governs their common invariants.
    }

    ProjectionRolePrecedence {
      Decision: Represent each RetrievedComponent with one highest-priority role:
      selected, dependency, importer, then cycle-member.

      Scope: Governs the agent-facing component role; excludes graph edges and
      component-owned links, which retain all selected relationships.

      Rationale: A single role keeps component grouping and ordering stable while the
      selected contract remains primary and each lower role conveys progressively
      less direct retrieval relevance.

      Consequences: Multiple raw relationships remain visible through links without
      duplicating a component or making its contract depend on evidence order.
    }

    ProjectionGlossary {
      Decision: Carry selected glossary-definition evidence on RetrievalProjection as
      ordered term-and-definition entries instead of making Markdown reread raw
      evidence.

      Scope: Governs agent-facing projection membership; excludes glossary selection,
      GlossaryFile authorship, and raw PurposeRetrievalResult shape.

      Rationale: RetrievalMarkdown takes the projection as its sole input, so omitted
      glossary entries cannot appear in Markdown without a second parse.

      Consequences: Projection fingerprints include glossary entries. Unused glossary
      rows remain absent.
    }

    AgentRetrievalProjection {
      Decision: Keep evidence-first PurposeRetrievalResult and component-first agent
      projection as independently versioned current protocols. The language migration
      uses sigil-purpose-retrieval/v2 and sigil-retrieval-projection/v2; no v1
      interpretation or forwarding compatibility layer remains.

      Scope: Governs agent-facing retrieval data and Markdown rendering; excludes raw
      retrieval membership, evidence, graph, ordering, JSON Lines, and compiler
      report protocols.

      Trade-offs: The projection adds a maintained schema, but avoids making every
      host reconstruct component, Tag, ownership, and link grouping.

      Design issues addressed: Flat evidence kinds expose source slices as peer
      content, producing repetitive Markdown that is difficult for people and agents
      to navigate.

      Discarded alternatives: Making every Markdown renderer infer groups from raw
      evidence was rejected. The current breaking protocol revisions preserve
      separate raw evidence and agent presentation responsibilities.

      Consequences: Hosts consume the current grouped projection while automation
      retains complete raw evidence and its independently defined fingerprint.

      Revisit when: A consumer requires a projection role, section, or relation that
      cannot be derived deterministically from purpose retrieval.
    }
  }

  cases {

    OwnershipTagScope {
      A consumer annotation selecting an imported Tag retains that exact
      provider-owned identity as scope on a consumer-owned OwnershipLink. An
      inline-only local Tag also remains selectable. Neither produces an authored
      local grouping in projected Interface Facets.

      An explicitly selected project-summary component uses the selected role and
      ordinary contract grouping; its filename creates no ancestry or module-context
      entry.
    }
    RetrievalProjection {
      A selected component with a MarkdownOutput local grouping Tag collects its
      interface grouping occurrences beneath MarkdownOutput while preserving each
      authored Facet and its source location.

      A selected component exposes its state, logic, constraints, decisions, and
      cases even when direct dependencies expose only their goal and interface.

      A component that is both a dependency and cycle member has dependency role; an
      importer that is also a cycle member has importer role.

      A graph edge whose endpoint has no projected component produces no
      component-owned link.

      An ownership annotation for a selected local grouping Tag becomes an
      OwnershipLink under that local grouping Tag with the annotation's
      repository-relative line and column.

      An implementation-purpose result contains advisory OwnershipLinks with a start
      location only and never embeds implementation-source slices.

      A dependency interface unit with a local grouping Tag identity occupies that
      named interface group on the dependency RetrievedComponent.

      Glossary-definition evidence becomes one projection glossary entry each and
      does not become a RetrievedComponent.
    }
  }
}
